WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.160
The SCP Foundation is responsible for containing
some of the most dangerous forces in the world.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.000
Without them, we’d all be at the mercy of
the Plague Doctor, walking through the world

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.600
and killing with a touch.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:18.000
Anyone could be snapped up by SCP-106 and
dragged to a painful death in his pocket dimension

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:18.640
lair.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.560
There would be no one to stop SCP-682 from
devouring all living things in sight, and

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:30.800
no one to hold back the dreaded Scarlet King
from breaching our world and destroying life

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:31.920
as we know it.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.560
We owe them a lot, for sure, and they’ve
earned at least a thank you card and an Edible

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.440
Arrangement, but containing the anomalies
of the world comes at a pretty steep cost.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.000
They’re essentially fighting a war against
a whole host of world-ending entities, and

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.520
when you’re at war, there are bound to be
casualties.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.480
For some people and creatures out there, the
most terrifying monster isn’t 096 trying

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.760
to swallow them whole for looking at its face,
or 173 just waiting for them to turn their

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.600
back so it can snap their neck.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.920
For the unfortunates that find themselves
in the wrong place at the wrong time, the

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.360
scariest monster in the world is the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.120
Foundation
itself.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.680
A decade ago, the SCP Foundation was attempting&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.520
to recapture SCP-682, which&nbsp;
had breached containment

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.560
and was tearing its way through the southern
Congo region.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.960
Unable to contain the monster by other means,
and desperate to stop it from killing any

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:31.040
more civilians, the Foundation decided to
implement some rather extreme measures.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:35.680
They deployed a variety of chemical agents
and poisonous gasses in an attempt to slow

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.640
the creature down, but they had no effect.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:43.680
As the enormous reptile stomped its way toward
a nearby river, with a highly populated village

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.880
waiting on the other side, the Foundation
made the decision to take things up a notch.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.520
They launched an aerial strike, deploying
several aircrafts to drop explosives on the

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.120
area around the river.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:59.680
They destroyed large portions of the riverbank,
but the environmental impact was considered

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.760
to be a necessary evil.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.800
When the smoke finally cleared, and the deafening
roars of the beast had gone quiet, they stopped

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:10.960
their bombing campaign and dispatched Foundation
operatives to the scene.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:16.480
There, they found the bones of SCP-682, which
were quickly brought into custody before the

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.640
creature could begin to heal itself.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:22.800
The mission was considered a success, and
they were ready to pull out all of their staff

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:27.440
and head back to the nearest Foundation Site,
when one officer spotted something floating

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:29.040
in the nearby river.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.480
It looked like a group of human corpses face
down in the water, their bodies badly burned.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.200
Concerned that civilians from a nearby village
had been inadvertently present for the bombing

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.320
campaign, a team of officers&nbsp;
was sent to investigate&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.840
the river more closely.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.800
What they found was not a group of dead humans,
but something else entirely.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:54.240
There were, all along the river bank and floating
in the water, approximately 212 specimens

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.120
of a previously unknown humanoid species.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.680
The bodies were clustered in groups of three
to five, appearing to belong to the same family

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.200
unit or social group.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:08.000
Many of them were frozen in positions of fear
or an attempt to defend themselves, with some

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.400
observing personnel comparing them to the
victims of the Pompeii eruption, stuck in

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.400
their final terrified moments.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.040
What appeared to be parents and children held
onto each other, some covered their faces,

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.120
others lay in a fetal position.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:25.760
It seemed that they had known something was
coming to kill them, but they did not have

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:29.280
the time or the understanding necessary to
escape it.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:33.520
Several of the bodies were removed from the
river for autopsy and examination, in order

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.000
to understand more about this new, possibly
already extinct, species.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.800
They were humanoid organisms&nbsp;
with an indeterminable&nbsp;

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.480
genus and species.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:48.320
They resembled tall, thin humans with absolutely
no body hair and elongated limbs.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:53.600
The most unusual aspect of the creatures was
in their mouths: their teeth were serrated

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.800
and sharp, resembling those of a crocodile.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.920
In spite of these monstrous teeth, an autopsy
revealed that there was no human flesh present

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.720
in any of the creatures’ stomachs, instead
suggesting a diet of fish, livestock, and

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.440
whatever else they could peacefully scavenge.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:14.400
Every last corpse was removed from the area
and incinerated, to prevent any civilians

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:17.520
from coming across them and asking questions.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.760
Just when the Foundation personnel were finally
packing up and getting ready to leave the

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.880
river once and for all, they heard something.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:30.320
It was a mournful sound, something between
a man bellowing, and a wild animal yelping

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:31.280
in pain.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:36.720
Something nearby was still very much alive,
and it was screaming.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:41.680
The officers followed the sound, and spotted
one surviving specimen of the crocodile people,

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.520
lying along the bank of the river.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:48.480
It was holding its face in its hands, curled
up into a ball near the water, and it was

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.000
wailing in agony.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:55.840
There were no visible injuries on the creature’s
body, but it was clearly extremely distressed.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:00.720
One officer attempted to approach the creature,
calling out to it that he meant no harm, and

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:02.640
wanted to get it some medical attention.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:06.880
It looked up at the officer with wide eyes,
and its cries went quiet.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:11.200
The officer grabbed his weapon, afraid that
the creature might suddenly rush him, but

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.760
instead, it ran into the river.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:18.800
It jumped into the water, plunging beneath
the surface, and began thrashing around.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:23.440
After a moment of watching it struggle, the
officer realized what was happening: the creature

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:25.600
was trying to drown itself.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:30.480
He abandoned protocol completely at that moment,
diving into the water and pulling the struggling

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:31.920
creature back to shore.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:37.200
It coughed up water for several minutes, all
the while trying to crawl back into the water.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.280
When the creature had finally calmed down,
it was brought into Foundation custody with

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:42.880
no further resistance.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.760
It appeared to be the last living member of
whatever strange human-crocodile hybrid species

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:51.840
was living in that river, and it was designated
SCP-6415.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:59.520
Since it was brought into Foundation custody,
SCP-6415’s behavior has been largely very

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:00.480
consistent.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:04.880
Some SCPs are constantly attempting to escape
from their containment or killing an endless

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:10.400
revolving door of D-Class personnel, but 6415
is not one of those anomalies.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:15.200
It is not aggressive, in spite of its crocodilian
characteristics, and it’s content to eat

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.200
the food provided by the Foundation.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:22.640
It is fed a diet of raw meat, mostly beef
and goat, which is provided fresh daily.

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.040
The Foundation was curious to see if the creature&nbsp;

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.840
could be pushed to be&nbsp;
aggressive if its circumstances

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:30.320
were made a little less comfortable.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:34.880
They deprived it of food for several days,
but it did not seem to notice or even care

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:38.960
much aside from occasionally looking at the
door to see if new food had come.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.600
They tried sleep deprivation next, blaring&nbsp;

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.160
a loud siren sound over&nbsp;
speakers in the containment

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:48.400
chamber any time the creature was observed
lying down or closing its eyes.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:54.080
It became listless and visibly exhausted but
did not act out violently at this either.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:58.160
After this testing, its ordinary feeding and
sleep schedule was resumed.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:03.440
For the most part, all that SCP-6415 does
is eat and sleep.

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:07.360
There is, however, one notable exception.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:14.400
At random intervals, SCP-6415 will begin to
cry, sobbing intensely and appearing to be

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.880
in a state of overwhelming distress.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:21.840
Its cries are so loud that they can be heard
from several halls away, and have caused hearing

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:24.320
damage to personnel in the room with it.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:28.400
There is no way to stop the creature from
crying once it has started, though providing

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:33.760
it with a hot cup of tea, a soft blanket,
or a hug from a particularly brave and eager

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:37.840
D-class has caused it to cry a bit more quietly.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:42.320
Once it is finished crying, after several
hours of non-stop weeping, it will lie down

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:46.080
on the ground and not cry anymore for weeks
at a time.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:52.240
For a time, SCP-6415 was considered to be
lacking human intelligence, and its containment

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.560
procedures were changed to reflect that.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:59.680
It was held in a standard humanoid containment
chamber in the light containment wing of Site

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.640
619, with soundproof walls.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:07.600
Because it displayed no threatening behavior,
it was considered unnecessary to have any

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:10.880
guards placed outside 6415’s chamber.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:15.440
However, after Incident 6415-01, the Foundation’s&nbsp;

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:18.240
understanding of the creature&nbsp;
changed dramatically.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:23.440
The Incident occurred when several D-Class
personnel were sent into 6415’s containment

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:27.040
chamber to feed it, and they found a harrowing
sight.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:31.760
On the wall of the chamber, the entity had
scratched a message with its fingernails.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:36.720
Its fingertips were bloodied and torn; its
hands noticeably wounded from what must have

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.320
been a great deal of effort.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:42.640
It did not acknowledge the personnel that
entered the room, instead, it just sat on

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:48.160
the floor, staring at its work on the wall,
cradling its injured hands and crying.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:53.280
Its shoulders shook with the force of its
sobs, and its tears fell to the ground, pooling

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:54.000
around it.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:58.160
The D-Class personnel were later unable to
report what they had seen without beginning

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:03.520
to cry themselves, but eventually calmed down
enough to report what the creature had written:

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:05.280
“Please bring them back.”

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:10.480
It was a desperate plea for the Foundation
to somehow reunite it with its lost family.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:14.960
They had previously thought the creature to
be a simple animal, incapable of understanding

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:18.480
its own reality or communicating through clear
language.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:23.360
This proved that the creature understood very
well what had happened to it, and was feeling

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.680
the loss of its loved ones fully.

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:30.320
One D-Class officer noticed a scrap of paper,
likely a piece of butcher paper from one of

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.760
the creature’s previous meals, with a picture
drawn on it.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:39.680
It was a crude sketch, but its subject was
easily recognizable: it was the Southern Congo

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:45.280
river where 6415 was first discovered, with
three creatures splashing in the water.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:51.200
The largest one resembled SCP-6415, and it
was swimming alongside a slightly smaller

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:56.560
adult of its species and a much smaller creature
that appeared to be a juvenile of the same

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:57.600
species.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:04.240
Context clues indicated that this was a drawing
of SCP-6415’s family, its partner, and their

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:05.040
child.

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:09.360
At first, the Foundation researchers were
uncertain who exactly the creature was referring

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:13.680
to in its initial message, but this drawing
made it perfectly clear.

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:15.840
It wanted its family back.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:20.640
It is uncertain whether or not the creature
is aware that its family is dead, but it clearly

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:25.840
feels their absence just the same and believes
the Foundation might have the power to end

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:26.880
its suffering.

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:31.760
Foundation personnel who were exposed to the
details of the Incident became inconsolable,

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:36.800
falling into a deep bout of depression brought
on by a sense of shame and responsibility.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:41.040
When counseling sessions proved ineffective,
the emotionally affected staff were given

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:46.240
amnestics to wipe their memory of the Incident,
and of 6415 altogether.

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:50.480
One employee, Research Assistant Cheryl Cruz,
attempted to release the creature from its

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:54.080
containment, insisting that it deserved to
roam free.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:56.560
However, when she opened&nbsp;
the door to its containment&nbsp;

00:10:56.560 --> 00:11:00.000
facility, the creature made no move to leave.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:05.200
It just stared at her, tears in its eyes,
as if it knew that it had nowhere else to

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:05.840
go.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:09.840
Research Assistant Cruz was given a powerful
amnestic, and relieved of her position at

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:10.800
the Foundation.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.280
Her current whereabouts are unknown.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:17.840
In order to prevent any more reckless behavior
from sympathetic staff, the message scratched

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:22.480
into the wall was painted over, and the sketch
recovered from its chamber was destroyed.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:26.960
But even if the memories and evidence of the
creature’s pain are gone, anyone walking

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:29.920
by its chamber can still hear it weeping.

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:35.280
It is uncertain what the containment procedures
for SCP-6415 will become.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:40.720
It is not simply an animal and clearly understands
language, though it appears to be incapable

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:41.680
of speech.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:46.080
If it could talk, whatever it said would surely
be heartbreaking.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:51.680
For now, the entity remains in its cell, serving
as a grim reminder of the guilt that weighs

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:53.760
on the Foundation’s conscience.

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:58.800
No matter what they do with 6415, they cannot
take back what they did.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:03.600
They cannot lift the weight of the creature’s
grief, or bring back its lost family.

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:10.320
It is the lone survivor, sitting in its Foundation
cell, weeping for its broken heart and begging

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:15.280
the Foundation for the one thing it can never
do: Bring them back.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:22.080
Now go check out “SCP-1762 - Where The Dragons
Went” and “SCP-348 - A Gift from Dad”

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:24.400
for more heart-wrenching SCP’s!

